   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 363 of the laws of 2010, amending the judiciary law relating to granting the chief administrator of the courts the authority to allow referees to determine applications for orders of protection during the hours family court is in session, in relation to the expiration date thereof; and to amend chapter 219 of the laws of 2002 amending the judiciary law relating to the judicial hearing officer pilot program and the powers of the chief administrator of the courts, in relation to extending the expiration of the provisions of such chapter",
    "basePrintNo": "S7351",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7351-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 363 of 2010; amd §2, Chap 219 of 2002",
    "lawSection": "Judiciary",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7351\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend chapter 363 of the laws of 2010, amending the\njudiciary law relating to granting the chief administrator of the\ncourts the authority to allow referees to determine applications for\norders of protection during the hours family court is in session, in\nrelation to the expiration date thereof; and to amend chapter 219 of\nthe laws of 2002 amending the judiciary law relating to the judicial\nhearing officer pilot program and the powers of the chief\nadministrator of the courts, in relation to extending the expiration\nof the provisions of such chapter\n\n PURPOSE OF BILL :\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend two Chapters of law which will\nexpire if they are not extended.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS OF BILL :\n\nSection one of the bill will extend for two years Chapter 363 of the\nLaws of 2010 which concerns the authority of referees in family court\nto adjudicate petitions for orders of protection requested ex parte\nand those issued on default at any time the court is in session;\n\nSection two of the bill extends for an additional two years Chapter\n219 of the Laws of 2002 which concerns a Judicial Hearing Officer\npilot program in family court and related authority to issue orders of\nprotection.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThese chapters of law will expire if not extended.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill, 2016.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
